      "mechanism_id": "cross_section_formula",
      "statement": "The partial scattering cross section sigma_{alpha,beta} is given by sigma_{alpha,beta} = (4 pi a_alpha / v_g) |Tbar(P,E+i0)|^2 Im[L_beta(P,E+i0)], where Tbar = -L^{-1}. For incoming dark waves (alpha=0), the total cross section sigma_0,tot = sum_beta sigma_0,beta diverges near critical points because v_g ~ sqrt(Delta E) and v_g^{-1} ~ Delta E^{-1/2}. The branching ratio sigma_0,beta/sigma_0,tot simplifies to Im[L_beta]/Im[L].",
